From 49948bf1271c878b5ffa09be7a610fc3442ca0df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Loukious <24696530+Loukious@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:42:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] wlan: free monitor buffers through their descriptor owner

When allocation of a monitor parent skb fails, release the receive buffer
through dp_rx_mon_buffer_free(). This selects the fragment or skb release
operation from the descriptor instead of treating its TLV data pointer
as an independently owned fragment.

Clear the local msdu pointer before entering the shared drop path, matching
the other monitor buffer disposal paths.

Port the matching kernel-tree source delta with the modules/ path prefix
removed.

Source-commit: c647d0904ac5b6e67b4ddc05e3650f8da0469d01
Signed-off-by: Loukious <24696530+Loukious@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c
index 1e0f251..7fe73b5 100644
--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c
@@ -372,7 +372,8 @@ dp_rx_mon_mpdu_pop(struct dp_soc *soc, uint32_t mac_id,
 					DP_STATS_INC(dp_pdev,
 						     replenish.nbuf_alloc_fail,
 						     1);
-					qdf_frag_free(rx_desc_tlv);
+					dp_rx_mon_buffer_free(rx_desc);
+					msdu = NULL;
 					dp_rx_mon_dest_debug("failed to allocate parent buffer to hold all frag");
 					drop_mpdu = true;
 					goto next_msdu;
-- 
